<body>
    <h1>Employee access matrix configuration CX</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h1 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-AllowableOptionsforPr=
imaryAccessAssignments">Allowable Options for Primary Access Assignments</h=
1>
<h2 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-FirmSetupRules">Firm Setup Ru=
les</h2>
<p>There are 3 assignable primary firm setups for employees:</p>
<ol>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b74d2d6f-a40d-45eb-83e0-a3639746541b"><strong>NBIN Intern=
al:</strong> access to any of the firm accounts under the NBIN business lin=
e; generally used by teams who are supporting clients, processing requests =
on their behalf, or managing a Middle / Back Office function for our firms<=
/li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"ba48b216-02f5-4242-a70d-4eb3aef55182"><strong>COR</strong=
>: an internal firm setup configured largely as an IB, for operational purp=
oses containing operational accounts and test accounts; some RR ranges are =
using for internal processing e.g. accounting adjustments and others are us=
ed solely for product / project testing purposes</li>
</ol>
<p>The intent of the primary CX profile is to reflect access required for t=
he job function of the user, so firm selection will be standardized against=
 the department selected. &nbsp;</p>
<p>A primary user profile for CX will have the firm pre-defined against the=
 job function.</p>
<h2 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-UserSetupRules">User Setup Ru=
les</h2>
<h2 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-CXiscurrentlyprimarilyarole-b=
asedmodelwhere:"><span style=3D"font-size: 14.0px;letter-spacing: 0.0px;">C=
X is currently primarily a role-based model where:</span></h2>
<ol>
 <li data-uuid=3D"cf6559e8-7bfd-46a9-a683-ae1f5cd210fb">A fixed feature acc=
ess profile is assigned to a user, and</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"5d3191d7-201d-49d2-b882-7d10399ce70f">A configurable data=
 access profile (i.e. RR codes) is assigned to work against those features.=
</li>
</ol>
<p>This model generally supports departmental access to CX.</p>
<h3 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-RoleProfileAssignment">Role P=
rofile Assignment</h3>
<p>There is a 1:1 departmental relationship with a given fixed profile setu=
p to ensure consistent access for each job function, and least privileges a=
re applied.</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"b99684b1-9175-4dc9-bd60-a763d1be5179">e.g. Trade Desk =3D=
 Manage Transactions</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"25de26b8-ecd6-4d65-8031-aed45c95b53b">e.g. Registered Pla=
ns team =3D Manage Service Requests</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1a411135-cbdf-49a8-8ef1-0cc59b179ac3">e.g. Sales team =3D=
 View-Only</li>
</ul>
<p>Allowable departments are as defined in the access matrix at the departm=
ent level (not only by transit).</p>
<h3 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-ModuleOverrides">Module Overr=
ides</h3>
<p>Manual "override" configurations are required around initial feature lau=
nches due limitations of the portal behavior - new features that are launch=
ed but hidden for internal users will still be selectable in the user setti=
ngs, and must be manually turned off each time a new profile is created or =
role changed.</p>
<h3 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-DataAccess">Data Access</h3>
<p>Corresponding to the purpose of the job function, RR codes would be assi=
gned as such:</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 54=
.9348%;">
  <colgroup>
   <col style=3D"width: 23.6532%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 76.3124%;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Firm</th>
    <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">RR Ranges</th>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">NBIN Internal</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Firm-level access for support / operational&=
nbsp;departments</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">COR</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>CNTA for access to live test accounts only</p>
     <p>(NB: COR accounts are also accessible within NBIN Internal for Oper=
ational teams)</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A specific client firm</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Custom; typically firm-level access for vali=
dators</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-AdditionalSettings">Additiona=
l Settings</h3>
<p>Linked ID's:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"baca617f-a9db-4066-8dbf-49806763e5de">R2, OSS ID's will n=
eed to be included once these ID's are setup and are optional to specify</l=
i>
</ul>
<p>Default module:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"2cb8826e-a971-4e49-8deb-1c9eff092fe3">Accounts for all us=
ers EXCEPT for those with a privileged user admin. role (see below)&nbsp;</=
li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-AllowableOptionsforAdditional=
AccessAssignments">Allowable Options for Additional&nbsp;Access Assignments=
</h1>
<h2 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-FirmSetupRules.1">Firm Setup =
Rules</h2>
<p>There are 3 assignable secondary firm setups for employees:</p>
<ol>
 <li data-uuid=3D"47fdbdd7-b143-4ab9-b5ed-afbb56ed3aab"><strong>NBIN Intern=
al:</strong> access to any of the firm accounts under the NBIN business lin=
e; generally used by teams who are supporting clients, processing requests =
on their behalf, or managing a Middle / Back Office function for our firms<=
/li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"64bbfcc8-d1df-4459-9903-3361a2133148"><strong>COR</strong=
>: an internal firm setup configured largely as an IB, for operational purp=
oses containing operational accounts and test accounts; some RR ranges are =
using for internal processing e.g. accounting adjustments and others are us=
ed solely for product / project testing purposes</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"55427e9d-b197-4fb9-8664-a830ab9d9676"><strong>A specific =
client firm</strong>: a live firm on the platform (temporary)</li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-UserSetupRules.1">User Setup =
Rules</h2>
<p>These additional profiles are dependent on its usage and therefore do no=
t have standard configurations.</p>
<h3 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-RoleProfileAssignment.1">Role=
 Profile Assignment</h3>
<p>Restrictions TBC.</p>
<h3 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-ModuleOverrides.1">Module Ove=
rrides</h3>
<p>Customizable</p>
<p><strong>Data Access</strong></p>
<p>Customizable</p>
<p><strong>Additional Settings</strong></p>
<p>Linked ID's:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d9ea43d5-f2ce-45c6-8932-b6fc4616f3ad">R2, OSS ID's will n=
eed to be included once these ID's are setup and are optional to specify; R=
2 ID's cannot be reused across profiles</li>
</ul>
<p>Default module:</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e7a4755f-0649-465c-92db-e7f54995e370">Accounts for all us=
ers&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"EmployeeaccessmatrixconfigurationCX-PrivilegedAccessAssignments">=
Privileged Access Assignments</h1>
<p>CX has roles that provides higher level access:</p>
<ol>
 <li data-uuid=3D"c92d851b-3ae9-4813-ba68-a39efb36624e">Manage Firm &amp; U=
ser</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"2dd23342-7007-4308-92d9-16cf6c7c4e83">Config Platform</li=
>
 <li data-uuid=3D"8d8e0eb8-d28b-456f-a075-27e17ca39640">TBC - superuser (F&=
amp;UM + Manage All)</li>
</ol>
<p>Privileged access profiles needs to be the primary profile in order to a=
pply the full lifecycle controls of IIQ.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
